.TH MW-VIEW 1 "2026-07-03" "MemoryWhale" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
mw-view \- render a single MemoryWhale memory as a local web page
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B mw-view
.br
.B mw-view
.I id
.RB [ --no-open ]
.br
.B mw-view session
.I id
.br
.B mw-view command
.I id
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B mw-view
reads the local SQLite store and writes a self-contained HTML page for one
recorded session or command run, then opens it in your browser. With no
arguments it lists the memories you can open. Local only; nothing is uploaded.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --no-open
Write the HTML file but do not launch a browser.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.BI "mw-view " id
Render the session or command run with that id and open it.
.TP
.BI "mw-view session " id
Render a recorded session.
.TP
.BI "mw-view command " id
Render a command run.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR mw (1),
.BR mw-serve (1),
.BR mw-recover (1)
